ion":{"commit_sha":"0d691ab76562d269704340265ffd1683b1e4a78f","position":"1785397155151574001-f1c73f98-32c8-4ccb-953c-3b13a47d2791"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"abcd22929ae38dbf4df0cc0cc06b75c6ce294730e5dc38ef9400830240e4ff54","event_uuid":"411ebbcc-2da0-4c4f-afcc-d367857b9781","position":{"commit_sha":"7486e0a667f30b6ec5544818674d2a30f1586503","position":"1785397498716048790-411ebbcc-2da0-4c4f-afcc-d367857b9781"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-220_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"d1ad70ed-ce91-4b63-9f32-e6b36aea17d4","comments":[],"created_at":1785384349215144001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"146bdd59-22e4-4688-b1a5-1fd9d964ad8c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"864e-25d4-be0f-4154"},{"link_uuid":"11711433-7d32-4436-ba12-19ba853c66c8","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f91b-2e95-0ca8-4f1b"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nBacktests over the 7-day population (153 tickets; 104 passed-plan FP set, 55 blocked-plan hit set) and a 200-ticket extended set support two deterministic floor additions. (R1) verification-presence: 1-4/104 marginal FPs, all 4 blocked-plan hits overlapped the real blocking findings. (R2) the P6 vague lexicon matches word prefixes with no trailing boundary (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_floor.py:458-477), so `clean` fires on \"cleanly\"/\"lint clean\"; the fixed rule measured 0 FPs across 304 passed plans. Operator approved both for blocking.\n\n## Approach\np6_ac_quality is monolithic and stays advisory, so both new blocking rules are implemented as SEPARATE DET checks with their own coverage entries rather than promotions inside P6: (R1) a new blocking check `p10_verification_presence`: a leaf plan passes if it has a `## Testing` or `## Verification` H2 section, OR >= 1 `- [ ]`/`- [x]` AC item that contains an inline code span (backtick-fenced token) or matches the verification-vocabulary regex `(?i)\\b(pytest|test_[a-z0-9_]+|make\\s+\\w+|rebar\\s+\\w+|git\\s+\\w+|grep\\b|assert\\w*|checked:|verif(?:y|ied|ies|ication)|exit\\s+code)\\b`. This vocabulary is exhaustive for the check — nothing else qualifies. (R2) a new blocking check `p11_ac_vagueness`: the fixed lexicon (both word boundaries; `clean` dropped; `etc.` kept; all other current _VAGUE_LEXICON terms kept) scanned over AC item lines only (det_operator_attested.ac_item_lines). Code-span handling: inline code-span positions are recorded on the ORIGINAL line before spans are blanked for matching; a lexicon hit inside a recorded span never fires, and an `etc.` occurrence whose start lies within 30 characters after a recorded span's end is exempt (a non-exhaustive enumeration of already-concrete examples). P6's advisory lexicon is updated to the same fixed matching so the two surfaces agree. Existing tests asserting P6-family posture are updated in the same change: tests/unit/test_clarity_floor.py, tests/unit/test_det_floor_operator_attested.py, and tests/unit/plan_review/test_det_citation.py (line 108 asserts `r.blocking is False` on a p6_ac_quality result — unaffected in behavior since P6 stays advisory, re-run to confirm). Documentation: docs/plan-review-gate.md has no DET-gate table; its deterministic-floor prose section is extended with P10/P11 descriptions. The criteria guide is generated from the LLM registry and does not cover DET checks — no regeneration applies. Alternative rejected: spec-by-example/riskiest-assumption floors — backtests showed no discrimination (76%/71% and 86%/80% fire rates on good vs blocked plans).\n\n## Scope\nsrc/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_floor.py, tests/unit/test_det_floor_clarity.py (new), tests/unit/test_clarity_floor.py, tests/unit/test_det_floor_operator_attested.py, tests/unit/plan_review/test_det_citation.py (confirm/adjust posture assertion), docs/plan-review-gate.md.\n\n## Testing\nUnit for R1: a plan whose ACs carry no code span and no vocabulary match and no Testing section blocks; one backticked-command AC passes; a \"checked:\" AC passes. Unit for R2 over the enumerated FP fixture lines transcribed from the backtest (each must NOT fire): \"`make lint` exits 0 (ruff + format check clean)\"; \"mypy --strict runs clean on the new module\"; \"the parser clean parses all fixture files\"; \"Clean preferred-schema responses round-trip\"; \"the close precheck sees a clean tickets-tracker HEAD\"; \"the core-wheel lane is clean after the split\"; \"the collector cleanly collects all retired events\"; \"stale worktrees are cleaned up by the janitor\"; \"run `git grep -n 'pattern' docs/ src/`, etc. and confirm no hits\"; \"Robustness: the simulated-stall test passes\". Positive cases (must fire): \"works properly\"; \"handles errors, etc.\" with no adjacent code span; \"reasonable performance\".\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] p10_verification_presence blocks a leaf plan with no code-span AC, no vocabulary-matching AC, and no Testing/Verification section, and passes each of the three qualifying forms (checked: `pytest tests/unit/test_det_floor_clarity.py`).\n- [ ] p11_ac_vagueness produces zero matches on the ten enumerated fixture lines and fires on the three enumerated positive cases (checked: parameterized test over the lines listed in Testing).\n- [ ] `clean` is absent from the blocking lexicon and the `etc.` span-proximity exemption uses original-line span positions (checked: unit tests).\n- [ ] P6 remains advisory and its existing posture assertions still hold (checked: the three updated/confirmed test files pass).\n- [ ] docs/plan-review-gate.md's deterministic-floor section documents P10 and P11 (checked: doc text assertion in the new test file).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_floor.py","reason":"R1 check + fixed lexicon"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_det_floor_clarity.py","reason":"new tests"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_clarity_floor.py","reason":"update posture assertions"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_det_floor_operator_attested.py","reason":"update posture assertions"},{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"document R1/R2"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","a492-3e46-ca44-40a5"],["relates_to","864e-25d4-be0f-4154"],["relates_to","f91b-2e95-0ca8-4f1b"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"a492-3e46-ca44-40a5","parent_status_uuid":"0e71747c-29c2-4142-b453-787aad66e8c3","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"49b8-0c3a-53c3-46ad","ticket_type":"story","title":"Clarity floor: blocking verification-presence check and boundary-fixed vague lexicon","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["92df70ec-c533-4320-b992-50b54318bb73","31178ab9-bbf3-4431-8942-e9945e5981a9","d463583a-5011-488e-80f3-f60fe8665e6b","a390cf8b-a6a2-43a7-be94-f43889015017","382a2132-306f-4bb9-a50a-c921a02d0476","be00c006-a5e1-4dbb-970b-b23c1d60e5de","0e71747c-29c2-4142-b453-787aad66e8c3","f1c73f98-32c8-4ccb-953c-3b13a47d2791","411ebbcc-2da0-4c4f-afcc-d367857b9781","146bdd59-22e4-4688-b1a5-1fd9d964ad8c","11711433-7d32-4436-ba12-19ba853c66c8"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785429494726535871,"uuid":"45ae09f8-9b6c-4cbd-835f-d6ca4598ae68"}